# busybox init. /init has already done the mounts and USB gadget setup.
# The shell gets root's home and session bus (below) the way a desktop login would.
::respawn:/bin/sh -c 'export HOME=/root XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/run/user/0 DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS=unix:path=/run/user/0/bus; exec /usr/sbin/telnetd -F -b 172.16.42.1 -l /bin/sh'
::respawn:/usr/sbin/udhcpd -f /run/chef/udhcpd.conf
::respawn:/bin/sh -c 'if [ ! -e /run/chef/dbus-helper-ready ]; then sleep 10; exit 1; fi; exec /usr/bin/dbus-daemon --system --nofork --nopidfile'
# A PAN link (bnep*) must not reach the root telnet on the USB subnet (Linux
# answers for 172.16.42.1 on any interface), the same rule wifi-usb-guard sets
# for wlan0. bluetoothd does not start without it.
::respawn:/bin/sh -c 'while [ ! -S /run/dbus/system_bus_socket ]; do sleep 1; done; iptables-legacy -w 5 -C INPUT -i bnep+ -d 172.16.42.0/24 -j DROP 2>/dev/null || iptables-legacy -w 5 -I INPUT 1 -i bnep+ -d 172.16.42.0/24 -j DROP || { echo "cyclo: BNEP ingress guard failed, bluetoothd not started" > /dev/kmsg; sleep 10; exit 1; }; exec /usr/lib/bluetooth/bluetoothd -n'
# Root's session bus at the standard XDG path, for session services such as
# obexd (bluez-obexd, D-Bus activated) and PipeWire run by hand, without
# dbus-run-session. Volatile.
::respawn:/bin/sh -c 'mkdir -p /run/user/0 && chmod 700 /run/user/0 || exit 1; export HOME=/root XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/run/user/0; exec /usr/bin/dbus-daemon --session --nofork --nopidfile --address=unix:path=/run/user/0/bus'
::once:/bin/sh -c 'exec /usr/bin/gps-up > /run/chef/log/gps-up.log 2>&1'
::respawn:/usr/bin/wifi-nm
# SSH on port 22 of every interface (USB, Wi-Fi, PAN), key login only:
# dropbear under chef-sshd, authorized keys baked into the image, host key on
# /data/v1/ssh (ephemeral in /run/chef/ssh when /data is not ours). The telnetd
# above stays as it is: the passwordless USB-only recovery shell.
::respawn:/usr/bin/chef-sshd
# GNSS on demand: idle until a client leases it on /run/chef/gps-manager.sock
# (`gps-manager hold map`), then runs the LOC session, gpsd and the NMEA
# pipeline on top of the gps-up modem; never starts or stops gps-up.
::respawn:/usr/bin/gps-manager
# Client-only NTP, no network command/server listener. The drift file is in
# /var/lib/chrony: /data/v1/chrony bound there by chef-storage when /data is
# ours, else the tmpfs directory (chronyd as `chrony` must own it either way).
::respawn:/bin/sh -c 'mkdir -p /run/chrony /var/lib/chrony && chown chrony:chrony /run/chrony /var/lib/chrony && chmod 700 /run/chrony /var/lib/chrony && exec /usr/sbin/chronyd -d -u chrony -f /etc/chrony/chrony.conf'
# Wall clock against the RTC on /data (chef-state): saved while chrony is
# synchronised, restored by /init on the next boot.
::respawn:/usr/bin/chef-state timekeeper
::respawn:/usr/bin/bt-up
# BLE sensors (heart rate, power, speed/cadence): pairs them, reconnects them
# during a client hold or a bounded 300 s window; notifications stay on
# /run/chef/blesensd.sock
# (`blesensd status|list|watch`); records via chef-state on /data/v1/blesens.
::respawn:/usr/bin/blesensd
# Side buttons: grabs the power/volume evdev nodes and publishes gestures on
# /run/chef/buttond.sock; with nothing claiming them a short power press toggles
# the screen-off flag /run/fblog.off (historical name), and power held 3 s (buzz
# at 1.5 s, long buzz at 3 s) then released runs `poweroff` -- the orderly
# way down through this init (::shutdown, SIGTERM to all, RB_POWER_OFF).
# The PMIC hard-resets on its own at ~8.7 s held. `buttond watch` to look.
::respawn:/usr/bin/buttond
# Battery: low-battery warn (15 %) / critical (5 %) and a clean poweroff when
# empty and unpowered or at 68 C, state in /run/chef/power (`powerd
# status`), the power_supply log in /data/v1/power (4 MiB + one rotation)
# when /data is ours, else in /run/chef/power (1 MiB), and the 44/42 C
# charge throttle on system_temp_level.
::respawn:/bin/sh -c 'if /usr/bin/chef-state ours; then exec /usr/bin/powerd -l /data/v1/power -L 4194304; else exec /usr/bin/powerd; fi'
# Sensors: sensors-up boots the ADSP through audio-up (no sensor needs the
# panel or the speaker), copies the registry out of persist (read-only, see
# docs/features/sensors.md) and supervises sensord, the SMGR client behind
# /run/chef/sensord.sock (`sensord list|status`). The UI claims the ambient
# light sensor only while the screen is on and Auto brightness or theme Auto
# is set. It exits when sensord does; the 10 s wait keeps a failing start
# from spinning. Log: /run/chef/log/sensors-up.log and kmsg; before each
# start the log is moved to /run/chef/log/sensors-up.log.1 when it is over
# 256 KiB. sensord runs without -v and with its stderr on /dev/null (its
# notes still reach kmsg), so the log holds only sensors-up's own lines:
# bounded by the rotation, about 512 KiB at most.
::respawn:/bin/sh -c 'f=/run/chef/log/sensors-up.log; [ "$(stat -c %s $f 2>/dev/null || echo 0)" -gt 262144 ] && mv -f $f $f.1; SENSORD_ARGS= SENSORD_STDERR=/dev/null /usr/bin/sensors-up >> $f 2>&1; sleep 10'
# The system UI (chef-settings: status bar, settings hub, Display page). It
# takes the panel through /run/fb0.lock, claims power.short from
# buttond (Back on a page, screen off on the hub) and picks up
# NetworkManager, BlueZ, gps-manager and /data whenever they appear. A boot
# with /run/fblog.off present stays dark. If it dies with the panel lit, the
# next start power-cycles the panel once so touch resumes (/run/fb0.lit,
# docs/features/ui-platform.md); a failed start
# waits 5 s first. Settings: /data/v1/ui/settings (or /run/chef/ui when /data is
# not ours). See docs/features/system-ui.md.
::respawn:/usr/bin/chef-settings
# A/B slot: mark boot_a successful once this boot has lasted 30 s, as
# Android's boot_control HAL did, so abl stops counting retries down (it
# would mark the slot unbootable after 7 boots). A build that dies earlier
# keeps counting and ends in fastboot. Logs to kmsg and
# /run/chef/log/abslot.log.
::once:/bin/sh -c 'sleep 30; exec /usr/bin/abslot mark-successful >/dev/null'
::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot
# chef-state first (last RTC offset, chronyd stopped so its drift file is
# written, last magnetometer bias), bounded so it cannot hold up the rest;
# then chef-storage makes /data read-only and detaches it.
::shutdown:/usr/bin/timeout -k 1 5 /usr/bin/chef-state shutdown
::shutdown:/usr/bin/chef-storage shutdown
::shutdown:/bin/umount -a -r
::restart:/bin/sh -c '/usr/bin/timeout -k 1 5 /usr/bin/chef-state shutdown; /usr/bin/chef-storage shutdown; exec /sbin/init'
